.TH nut_webgui 1 "__PLACEHOLDER_DATE" "__PLACEHOLDER_VERSION" "nut_webgui User Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
nut_webgui \- Simple NUT Web interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
nut_webgui [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<LISTEN_ADDRESS>\fR]
           [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-base\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-default\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-config\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-allow\-env\fR]
           [\fB\-\-anonymous\-metrics\fR \fI<true|false>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-server\-key\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR]
           [\fB\-\-with\-auth\fR \fI<AUTH_FILE_PATH>\fR]
           [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-worker\-count\fR \fI<NUMBER>\fR]
           [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
           [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.YS

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B nut_webgui
is a modern alternative to
.MR upsstats.cgi 8 .
See
.MR nut_webgui 7
for the additional config files and features.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", "\-\-listen
Listen address for the HTTP server. Default is 
.IR 0.0.0.0.
.TP
.BR \-p ", "\-\-port
Port used by the HTTP server. Default is
.IR 9000.
.TP
.BR \-\-base\-path
Override HTTP server base path. Default is 
.IR /.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level
Log level for the HTTP server. Default is 
.IR info.
.TP
.BR \-\-default\-theme
Web UI default theme.
.TP
.BR \-\-config\-file
Set
.IR config.toml
path
.TP
.BR \-\-allow\-env
Allow application to load configuration from environment variables.
.TP
.BR \-\-anonymous\-metrics
Set anonymous access on 
.IR /metrics
endpoint, ignored when auth is disabled.
Default is
.IR false.
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-key
Set private server key value. Default is auto-generated random value.
.TP
.BR \-\-with\-auth
Enable authentication with
.IR user.toml
file.
.TP
.BR \-\-worker\-count
Set HTTP server worker count.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help menu and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
nut_webgui can read environment variables for configuration. In order to use
environment variables, the user must explicitly enable
.IR \-\-allow\-env
flag.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__CONFIG_FILE
Set
.IR config.toml
path
.TP
.BR NUTWG__DEFAULT_THEME
Set Web UI default theme.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__LOG_LEVEL
Set log level.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__SERVER_KEY
Set private server key value.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__AUTH__ALLOW_ANONYMOUS_METRICS
Set anonymous access on
.IR /metrics
endpoint, ignored when auth is disabled.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__AUTH__USERS_FILE
Enable authentication with
.IR user.toml
file.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__HTTP_SERVER__BASE_PATH
Set HTTP server base path.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__HTTP_SERVER__LISTEN
Set HTTP server listen address.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__HTTP_SERVER__PORT
Set HTTP server port.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__HTTP_SERVER__WORKER_COUNT
Set HTTP server worker count.

.PP
The following environment variables can be used to configure a single upsd
server without requiring an additional config file.

.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__ADDRESS
Set UPSD address.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__MAX_CONNECTION
Set allowed maximum connection for UPSD client.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__NAME
Set namespace for the `NUTWG__UPSD__*` environment variables.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__PASSWORD
Set UPSD password.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__POLL_FREQ
Non-critical ups variables update frequency in seconds.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__POLL_INTERVAL
Critical ups variables (`ups.status`) update interval in seconds.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__PORT
Set UPSD port.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__TLS_MODE
Configure TLS mode between UPSD and client.
.TP
.BR NUTWG__UPSD__USERNAME
Set UPSD username.

.SH CAVEATS
.PP
nut_webgui's x86_64 and ARMv8 builds use Mimalloc v2 as the memory allocator.
The change improves overall performance, especially for the self-contained Musl
builds. However, Mimalloc uses thread-local segments, which can significantly
increase memory usage on systems with high CPU count.
.PP
Recommended action is limiting
.IR \-\-worker\-count
to a reasonable value between 1 and 4.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful server exit.
.TP
.B 1
Unrecoverable error, configuration error

